A track is one sequential line of work, so steps within it never overlap; simultaneous work belongs on separate tracks. Each step has exactly one duration kind: fixed with seconds, variable with minimum, maximum, and default seconds, or indefinite until the cook ends it. A start trigger connects a step to the program clock or another step through programStart, programStartOffset, afterStep, afterStepWithBuffer, manual, onAbort, or compound. Step IDs must be unique across the entire program, not merely within a track. Every task used by a step needs a matching resource constraint, whose maxConcurrent value limits shared resources such as an oven, burner, or cook. Repeated work belongs on one replicated step rather than copied steps, with each-instance and all-instance dependencies as needed, and maxInFlight when a downstream holding area has limited capacity.

The recipe needs these resource constraints:

- `oven`: `maxConcurrent: 1` — one oven.
- `burner`: `maxConcurrent: 1` — one burner.
- `sheet-pan`: `maxConcurrent: 2` — two sheet pans.
- `prep`: `maxConcurrent: 1` — one cook performing preparation, sauce, salad, and plating.

One person is working: `actors: 1`.

```json
{
  "acknowledgement": "Tracks are sequential lines of work; one duration kind is used per step; triggers link steps; stepIds are unique across the whole program; every task needs a matching resource constraint; repeated work uses one replicated step with instance-aware dependencies and optional maxInFlight.",
  "resourceConstraints": [
    {
      "task": "oven",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "burner",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "sheet-pan",
      "maxConcurrent": 2
    },
    {
      "task": "prep",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    }
  ],
  "actors": 1
}
```
